WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.347
You cut a sandwich into two
parts. They must be the same size.

2
00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:12.561
Fair means the two pieces are
equal. That is a fraction.

3
00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:15.662
Here is a paper bar.
Cut it into four parts.

4
00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:19.458
These four parts are all the
same size. They are quarters.

5
00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:23.439
Now look at this bar. One piece
is much wider than the others.

6
00:00:23.659 --> 00:00:27.421
Four pieces, but not equal. So
not one of them is a quarter.

7
00:00:27.921 --> 00:00:31.218
A fraction has two numbers.
Here is three quarters.

8
00:00:31.438 --> 00:00:36.407
The bottom number is four. The
whole is cut into four equal parts.

9
00:00:36.627 --> 00:00:40.482
The top number is three. That
is how many parts you take.

10
00:00:40.702 --> 00:00:44.324
So shade three of the four
parts. Three quarters.

11
00:00:44.824 --> 00:00:47.657
A fraction can be part
of a group of things.

12
00:00:47.877 --> 00:00:51.546
Here are twelve apples. Share
them between four children.

13
00:00:51.766 --> 00:00:54.784
One each, round and round,
until they are all gone.

14
00:00:55.004 --> 00:00:58.069
Everyone gets three
apples. None is left over.

15
00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:02.190
One share out of four is a quarter.
A quarter of twelve is three.

16
00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:07.286
Half is the same idea. Eight sweets
shared between two is four each.

17
00:01:07.786 --> 00:01:11.409
Amina has twenty shillings.
She spends a quarter of it.

18
00:01:11.629 --> 00:01:15.669
Twenty shared between four is
five. She spends five shillings.

19
00:01:15.889 --> 00:01:19.372
There are twelve eggs. Three
quarters of them are brown.

20
00:01:19.592 --> 00:01:23.168
A quarter of twelve is three.
So three quarters is nine.

21
00:01:23.668 --> 00:01:27.151
Two fractions can be worth
exactly the same amount.

22
00:01:27.371 --> 00:01:30.761
Here is one half of the bar.
Under it are two quarters.

23
00:01:30.981 --> 00:01:34.371
They reach the same place.
One half is two quarters.

24
00:01:34.591 --> 00:01:38.910
Two quarters has bigger numbers.
It is not a bigger amount.

25
00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:43.681
And one half is bigger than one
quarter. More pieces, smaller pieces.

26
00:01:44.181 --> 00:01:47.339
Put quarters together and
you just count the parts.

27
00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:50.624
One quarter and two quarters
make three quarters.

28
00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:54.699
The bottom number stays four.
The pieces are still quarters.

29
00:01:54.919 --> 00:01:59.098
Four quarters fill the whole
pizza. That is one whole.

30
00:01:59.318 --> 00:02:03.312
Add one more quarter. Five quarters
is one whole and one quarter.

31
00:02:03.812 --> 00:02:07.713
A fair share is an equal
share. Always check the parts.

32
00:02:07.933 --> 00:02:12.623
The bottom number counts the parts.
The top counts the ones you take.

33
00:02:12.843 --> 00:02:16.419
A quarter of twelve is three.
Two quarters is one half.

34
00:02:16.639 --> 00:02:20.819
Four quarters make one whole. Now
go and share something fairly.
